{
  "version": 1,
  "about": "Golden cases for the rating normalizer: the US label each engine's channel rules read for a rating from another country. Read by scripts/nostalgex-rating-smoke.mjs (scripts/nostalgex-channel-filter.cjs usContentRating, web tuner and Docker; npm run test:ratings), Nostalgex/NostalgexTests/RatingGoldenTests.swift (ContentRating.usLabel, Apple TV) and roku/tests/RatingGoldenTests.brs (NxUsContentRating, copied to tests/vectors/ by gen-vectors.mjs). `raw` is the rating as the server sends it (null for none), `type` the item type (an episode gets a TV label, anything else a film label), `us` what the rules must read. A US label, an empty rating and anything not recognised come back unchanged. The node test also fails if a label in the engine's tables has no case here, so a new label needs a case before it ships.",
